        <p class="lead">Keith Dunstan wrote his 'A Place in the Sun' column for <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sun_News-Pictorial">The Sun News-Pictorial</a> from 1958 to 1978.</p>
        <p>The column ran in the paper from its first edition in 1922, but it was Keith who made it his own for twenty years, filing daily dispatches on Melbourne life, wine, food, suburbia and the wider Australian experience. The articles held here are transcribed from physical clippings.</p>
